Normal lymph node tissue shows distinct cortical follicles with pale germinal centers and darker mantle zones, intervening paracortex with mixed small lymphocytes, thin fibrous trabeculae, and vascular sinuses; staining yields basophilic nuclei and eosinophilic cytoplasm.
Patch shows well‑preserved lymph node architecture with round follicles and pale germinal centers, darker mantle zones, packed small lymphocytes in cortex and paracortex, medullary cords and sinuses with scattered histiocytes and occasional plasma cells.
A lymph node patch shows densely packed, small dark basophilic nuclei in cortex with paler germinal centers, interspersed paracortical zones of slightly looser cellularity, and medullary cords/sinuses with variable eosinophilic stroma.
Normal lymph node patches show well-organized nodular architecture with pale germinal centers surrounded by darker mantle zones, densely basophilic lymphocyte-rich paracortex, occasional sinusoids appearing as clear pale spaces, and scattered small blood vessels.
Normal lymph node patch shows organized cortex with round pale germinal centers and darker mantle zones, interspersed medullary cords and sinuses; cellular density, follicle size, and sinus prominence commonly vary between patches.
Normal lymph node patches show lobulated cortex with round to ovoid follicles, pale germinal centers surrounded by darker mantles, a slightly denser paracortex, open pale sinuses and variable numbers of small blood vessels and adipose trabeculae.
A normal lymph node patch shows rounded follicles with paler germinal centers and darker mantle zones, compact interfollicular lymphoid tissue with small dark nuclei, thin-walled vessels and occasional sinus spaces, with variable staining intensity.
Normal lymph node histology shows densely packed small basophilic lymphocyte nuclei with paler germinal centers, rounded follicles, delicate fibrovascular septa and sinus spaces; variations include follicle size, cellular density, staining intensity and minor adipose or stromal presence.
lymph node WSI patch displays round to oval follicles with pale germinal centers and darker mantle zones, intervening paracortex of small, densely packed lymphocytes, thin capsule, and open sinuses with occasional pigmented or granular debris.
Lymph node histology shows rounded follicles with pale germinal centers, compact dark mantle zones, interfollicular paracortex of small lymphocytes, sinuses with occasional macrophages, thin capsule and variable vascularity; size and density vary.
